// Stands in for the OpenOrbis SDK's <concepts>, which is a synopsis-only stub in libc++ 11: the
// header exists, declares nothing, and every `std::same_as` in ZenKit is an error. Found ahead of
// the SDK's copy by -I on this directory. NOT a product fix - see ps4_cxx20_shim.h.
//
// ⚠ ONE LINE ON PURPOSE. The definitions used to be duplicated here verbatim from
// ps4_cxx20_shim.h under a DIFFERENT include guard, so a TU that got the force-include and then
// wrote `#include <concepts>` compiled both copies and failed with 21 redefinitions. Concepts
// cannot be redeclared, and two guards whose only job is to prevent that cannot do it while they
// are not the same guard. Reproduced in one command:
//
//   clang++ -std=c++20 -fsyntax-only -I ps4/cxx20shim \
//           -include ps4/cxx20shim/ps4_cxx20_shim.h tu.cpp
//
// It built only because nothing in the tree includes <concepts> directly today - and ZenKit, the
// reason this shim exists at all, is exactly what would start.
#include "ps4_cxx20_shim.h"
